Package: fortvine
Type: Package
Title: Vine Copulas Computed by the 'fortvine' Fortran Library
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: person("Shahab Aldin", "Shojaeezadeh", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
    email = "shahab@uni-kassel.de")
Description: Bindings to 'fortvine', a vine-copula library written in Fortran
    with 'OpenMP'. Pair-copula densities, distribution functions, h-functions
    and their inverses for 111 families, including the nonparametric
    transformation local-likelihood and Bernstein estimators; maximum
    likelihood fitting and family selection with observation weights; vine
    selection by the algorithm of Dissmann et al. (2013)
    <doi:10.1016/j.csda.2012.08.010> for pair-copula constructions (Aas et al.
    2009 <doi:10.1016/j.insmatheco.2007.02.001>), with discrete margins, the
    vine criterion 'mBICv' and automatic truncation and thresholding of Nagler
    et al. (2019) <doi:10.1016/j.jmva.2019.03.004>; non-simplified vines, vine
    densities and Rosenblatt transforms are all computed by the Fortran code
    through its C interface; the R functions only convert arguments and wrap
    the results. Function names follow the 'rvinecopulib' package.
License: GPL (>= 3)
URL: https://bluerrror.github.io/fortvine/, https://github.com/Bluerrror/fortvine
BugReports: https://github.com/Bluerrror/fortvine/issues
Encoding: UTF-8
Imports: stats
SystemRequirements: a Fortran compiler with a C preprocessor (gfortran)
NeedsCompilation: yes
